Steps to Create the Flights KPI Dashboard
1. Discovering of data
Searched for tables in your FLIGHTS.KPI schema
Found the FLIGHT_KPIS table with columns: WINDOW_START, ORIGIN_COUNTRY, TOTAL_FLIGHTS, AVG_VELOCITY, ON_GROUND, LOAD_TIME
2. Checked Snowflake environment
Confirmed your warehouse: COMPUTE_WH
Found available compute pool: SYSTEM_COMPUTE_POOL_CPU
3. Created the project folder /flights-dashboard/ with 4 files:
4. Built the app logic (streamlit_app.py)
Connected to Snowflake using st.connection("snowflake")
Created a cached query to compute aggregate KPIs (total flights, avg velocity, on-ground, country count)
Created a cached query for time-series data grouped by WINDOW_START
Displayed 4 metric cards using st.metric()
Added 2 line charts (flights over time, velocity over time)
Added a "Refresh Data" button that clears the cache and reruns
5. Run it
Open streamlit_app.py in the Workspace and click Run
